.nh
.TH "PB-MACHINE-RENAME" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-machine-rename - Rename a machine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb machine rename <machine> <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Rename a machine

.PP
Change the display name of one enrolled machine. The enrollment identity and grants stay attached to the machine; callers should use the returned name for future selection.

.PP
Machines are account enrollments with independent names, capabilities, and revocation state. Changes target the selected machine, while pb setup configures the current machine. Revocation disconnects an enrollment rather than just hiding it from the list.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rename

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-machine(1)\fP
